---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PERSON_ID, SITE, WEBSITE_ID } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="About Tawanda Moyo — Engineer & Writer in Harare"
  description="Tawanda Moyo is a software engineer and technical writer in Zimbabwe: SpiderMonkey contributor, now working on AI safety and the Africa Compute Tracker."
  includePersonSchema
  schema={[{ '@type': 'ProfilePage', '@id': `${SITE}/about/#page`, url: `${SITE}/about/`, name: 'About Tawanda Moyo', mainEntity: { '@id': PERSON_ID }, isPartOf: { '@id': WEBSITE_ID } }]}
>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
    <p>
      I am an engineer and writer interested in systems - human and machine - and how they interact. 
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      No description is equal in difficulty, or certainly in usefulness, to the description of oneself. One must spruce up, present oneself in an orderly arrangement, if one wants to go out in public. Well, I am constantly making myself presentable, for I am constantly describing myself.
      <br />
      - Michel de Montaigne, Essays, "Of Practice," Book II, Chapter 6
    </blockquote>

    <p>Difficult as it is to describe oneself, let me try.</p>

    <p>
      I grew up in rural Zimbabwe, where I attended a Catholic high school. Later I attended the University of Zimbabwe, studying Mechanical Engineering. There, I was involved in student politics, and I started thinking seriously about how technology can be a tool for good.
    </p>

    <p>
      After that I studied Electronic Engineering at the Harare Institute of Technology. I most enjoyed the courses on programming, microcontrollers, embedded systems, robotics, and artificial intelligence. There I learned to design systems from the ground up, with hardware constraints in mind.
    </p>

    <p>
      I then worked as a Technical Writer for TalkJS, a Dutch startup, where I wrote documentation for their API and SDKs.
    </p>

    <p>
      Since then I have been a software engineer working on web applications. I have also worked on open source projects, including Matrix, Policy Engine, and the WHATWG HTML standard.
    </p>

    <p>
      These days I am moving toward AI safety - compute governance,
      evaluations, and forecasting. I have done several AI Safety courses (BlueDot: AI Alignment, AGI Strategy, ENAIS: AI Governance 101 & 201), and attended the ML4Good (technical
      track) bootcamp in 2026, and I maintain <a href="https://africacomputetracker.org">Africa Compute
      Tracker</a>. I care about this
      partly because I write from a place that has already lived through
      several kinds of quiet disempowerment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Montaigne asked <em>que sais-je?</em> - what do I
      know? - and I try to build and write in that spirit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Feel free to <a href="mailto:moyotawanda@gmail.com">email</a>; I
      read and reply to every one.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
